# Notifications & Ops

## Slack behavior

- **On tap**: immediate per-slot message (`buildToggleMessage`) — not a full summary
- **Scheduled**: code-block summary at 9, 11, 1, 3, 5, 6 PM `America/New_York`; dedupe one per hour
- All Slack posts append `<DASHBOARD_URL|Dashboard>` link
- Slot times are office-local; `isPastSlot()` and `todayStr()` use `OFFICE_TZ` (not pod UTC)

## Toggle logging

Every successful toggle logs one line:

```text
toggle pk 13:30 add
toggle pk 13:30 remove
```

Match Slack message times to these lines in pod logs.

## Debugging Slack posts

```bash
oc logs deployment/ping-pong -n pk-individual --timestamps --tail=50
```

- No toggle log line → likely scheduled summary or Slack webhook retry, not a tap
- `trust proxy` is set to `1` for OpenShift ingress (rate limiter uses X-Forwarded-For)

## OpenShift deploy

```bash
oc start-build ping-pong --from-dir=. --follow -n pk-individual
oc rollout restart deployment/ping-pong -n pk-individual
```

Namespace: `pk-individual`. Do not `oc apply` deployment.yaml blindly — live env has `SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL` set via `oc set env`.
